WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.190 --> 00:00:08.615
Welcome to CSC-225, Advanced Python Programming,
taught by Professor Harris

2
00:00:08.615 --> 00:00:11.390
Williams at Bunker Hill Community College.

3
00:00:11.390 --> 00:00:15.065
I'm glad you're here, and I'm excited to help you
take your Python skills to the

4
00:00:15.065 --> 00:00:20.740
next level. This course is fully online and
asynchronous, so you can learn on your

5
00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:25.603
own schedule. By the end, you'll be able to design
and test Python programs that

6
00:00:25.603 --> 00:00:30.570
solve practical problems, and analyze data and build
web applications.

7
00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:32.715
Here's what you'll learn along the way.

8
00:00:32.715 --> 00:00:34.502
The course has seven modules.

9
00:00:34.502 --> 00:00:36.840
Most modules run for two weeks.

10
00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:41.545
The final module continues through December 18, when
the course ends.

11
00:00:41.965 --> 00:00:46.240
In Module 1, Data Structures, you'll choose and use
lists, tuples, sets, and

12
00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:48.453
dictionaries to organize your data.

13
00:00:48.453 --> 00:00:52.665
Module 2, Advanced OOP and Polymorphism, builds on
that.

14
00:00:52.665 --> 00:00:57.095
You'll design reusable classes and use inheritance
to share behavior.

15
00:00:57.615 --> 00:01:02.440
In Module 3, Concurrency, you'll manage multiple
tasks with threads, processes,

16
00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:07.765
and subprocesses. Then Module 4, Data Analytics, is
where you'll clean, analyze,

17
00:01:07.765 --> 00:01:10.970
and visualize data with Python libraries.

18
00:01:11.315 --> 00:01:16.015
Module 5, Decorators and Context Managers, teaches
you to extend function behavior

19
00:01:16.015 --> 00:01:21.715
and manage resources safely. In Module 6, Web APIs
with FastAPI, you'll build web

20
00:01:21.715 --> 00:01:24.640
services that validate requests and work with data.

21
00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:28.440
And the course wraps up with Module 7, Django, where
you'll build a browser-based

22
00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:31.270
notes application backed by a database.

23
00:01:31.590 --> 00:01:33.515
So, what does a typical module look like?

24
00:01:33.515 --> 00:01:36.690
Start by reading and watching the Learning
Materials, run the examples and

25
00:01:36.690 --> 00:01:39.240
complete practice, then move on to the Deliverables.

26
00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:42.840
Each module includes an assignment, and there's also
a discussion in each module.

27
00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:47.015
You can resubmit coding assignments as many times as
you need through December 18.

28
00:01:47.015 --> 00:01:51.020
At the end of the course, there's a Final Project
that brings everything together.

29
00:01:51.365 --> 00:01:53.040
Now let's look at where your work happens.

30
00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:57.040
Everything lives in Canvas. Click Modules in the
left-side menu to see each module

31
00:01:57.040 --> 00:02:00.440
laid out. At the top of each module, you'll find
your Learning Materials.

32
00:02:00.440 --> 00:02:03.815
These include Jupyter notebooks in Grader Than
Workspace, with a tutorial for

33
00:02:03.815 --> 00:02:06.390
Django. There's nothing to install on your computer.

34
00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:09.252
Below that, you'll see the Deliverables section with
your assignment and

35
00:02:09.252 --> 00:02:14.903
discussion. To access your coding workspace, click
Grader Than in the Canvas menu.

36
00:02:14.903 --> 00:02:19.265
This opens Grader Than Workspace, where you'll write
and run your Python code.

37
00:02:19.265 --> 00:02:23.602
For coding activities configured for automatic
grading, the autograder can provide

38
00:02:23.602 --> 00:02:26.120
feedback to guide your revisions.

39
00:02:26.490 --> 00:02:27.577
Here are a few tips.

40
00:02:27.577 --> 00:02:29.340
Stay on the two-week pace.

41
00:02:29.340 --> 00:02:32.678
It keeps the material fresh and gives you time to
ask questions.

42
00:02:32.678 --> 00:02:35.940
Use the Question Board in Canvas whenever something
comes up.

43
00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:38.553
And remember, Professor Williams is here to help.

44
00:02:38.553 --> 00:02:42.195
Book office hours through the link on the course
home page.

45
00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:47.270
You've got this. Welcome to Advanced Python
Programming, and let's get started.

